WEBVTT

0
00:00:06.949 --> 00:00:09.060
The design phase covered the objectives,

1
00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:09.670
content,

2
00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:10.420
activities,

3
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.180
assessments,

4
00:00:11.189 --> 00:00:12.550
and teaching methods.

5
00:00:12.989 --> 00:00:15.890
Now it's time to turn those plans into something real.

6
00:00:17.229 --> 00:00:20.030
The development phase is where all of that gets built,

7
00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:20.809
organized,

8
00:00:20.829 --> 00:00:23.379
and made ready for learners and facilitators.

9
00:00:23.709 --> 00:00:24.950
Here's what that includes.

10
00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:28.450
First up are the instructional materials.

11
00:00:28.659 --> 00:00:30.079
Using an authoring tool,

12
00:00:30.489 --> 00:00:32.610
designers build the actual lessons,

13
00:00:33.009 --> 00:00:33.569
videos,

14
00:00:33.689 --> 00:00:34.880
interactive activities,

15
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:35.799
knowledge checks,

16
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:36.909
and assessments.

17
00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:42.090
Everything here ties back to the design plan and supports the learning objectives.

18
00:00:43.369 --> 00:00:45.490
Then there's the facilitator guide.

19
00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:49.009
Basically everything a facilitator needs to run the training

20
00:00:49.439 --> 00:00:49.930
objectives,

21
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:50.450
timing,

22
00:00:50.729 --> 00:00:51.770
discussion questions,

23
00:00:52.009 --> 00:00:53.169
activity instructions,

24
00:00:53.409 --> 00:00:53.810
materials,

25
00:00:53.889 --> 00:00:55.729
and notes on what to watch for.

26
00:00:56.049 --> 00:00:57.229
When it's done well,

27
00:00:57.409 --> 00:01:00.439
the training runs the same way no matter who's leading it.

28
00:01:00.729 --> 00:01:01.630
And lastly,

29
00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:03.520
if the instruction calls for it,

30
00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:05.449
a slide deck gets built too.

31
00:01:06.669 --> 00:01:09.879
Slides are useful for introducing key ideas,

32
00:01:10.279 --> 00:01:11.500
explaining concepts,

33
00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:12.839
showing examples,

34
00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:15.160
or guiding learners through an activity.

35
00:01:15.889 --> 00:01:17.169
Like the other materials,

36
00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:18.599
they need to be clear,

37
00:01:18.809 --> 00:01:19.589
organized,

38
00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:20.849
and easy to follow.